CBR  tests were performed according to ASTM D1883-07 ε2  [ 37 ] to estimate the stress-penetration response and the  CBR  value of both exhausted sands. Three specimens of each exhausted sand were tested. The specimens were prepared using the optimum water content and considering method C of the modified Proctor test [ 35 ], without soaking process. The test apparatus included a load frame with a 100 kN mechanical device, a 20 kN load cell, and a linear variable differential transformer (LVDT) with 25 mm range. Three annular plates, each with a weight of 24.52 N, were applied before the beginning of the test, to apply a constant surcharge to the specimen upper surface. The test was performed using a 50 mm diameter plunger and an axial displacement rate of 1.27 mm/min. Equation  3  was used to estimate the  CBR  value, considering the ratio between the stress measured for a penetration  x  (2.54 or 5.08 mm),  σ x , and the stress measured for a penetration x obtained for the standard material,  σ x, s  (6900 kPa or 10300 kPa, respectively). 3 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
