Giroud and Han [ 20 ,  21 ] design method was applied to estimate the base layer height for the different unpaved road solutions analysed. The method was developed and experimentally calibrated to estimate the base layer height (Eq.  5 ) for unpaved roads, with or without a geosynthetic reinforcement. The method considers soil-geosynthetic interaction, properties of the geosynthetic and of the base layer material, and effects and characteristics of the load applied. Relevant parameters are:  CBR  of the base layer ( CBR BL );  CBR  of the foundation layer ( CBR FL ); modulus ratio factor ( f E ); factor between undrained shear strength and  CBR FL  ( f C ); base layer height ( h ); geogrid aperture stability modulus ( J ); bearing capacity mobilization coefficient ( m ); bearing capacity factor ( N C ); number of passes of axle ( N ); wheel load ( P ); radius of equivalent tire contact area ( r ). 5 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
