This design method is applicable if the following conditions are met: the reinforcement is a geogrid or a geotextile; the foundation soil is assumed as a saturated fine soil, loaded under undrained conditions; it’s the  CBR  value of the foundation soil is less than 5%; the allowable rut depth ( s ) is between 50 mm and 100 mm; a minimum value of base layer height is defined, considering the rut depth and radius of equivalent tire contact area ( r ) obtained from Eq.  6  (defined by the method); the quality of the base layer soil must be sufficient to prevent failure. Based on the definition established by the US Army Corps of Engineers [ 38 ], herein and for the purpose of this study, an allowable rut depth of 75 mm is assumed. The modulus ratio factor ( f E ), Eq.  7 , is estimated considering the limited modulus ratio of the base layer to that of the foundation soil ( R E ), Eq.  8 . The bearing capacity coefficient ( m ) is determined from Eq.  9  considering the allowable rut depth ( s ), a factor ( f s ) equal to the rut depth, 75 mm, the height of the base layer ( h ) and the radius of equivalent tire contact area ( r ). 6 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
